# The keyportal image's build context is this whole directory (see
# docker-compose.yml), because its Dockerfile must COPY both keyportal/
# and onboarding/. Everything else here is compose-mounted config for
# other services and has no business inside a Python image -- and two
# entries are live SECRETS, which must never end up in a build layer or
# in the daemon's context upload.
#
# Deny by default, then allow back exactly the two directories the
# Dockerfile names. A default-allow list would silently start shipping
# whatever somebody adds to this directory next, including the next .env
# variant.
*
!keyportal/requirements.txt
!keyportal/app.py
!onboarding/setup-macos-linux.sh
!onboarding/setup-windows.ps1

# Restated explicitly, even though `*` above already covers them, because
# these are the two files whose accidental inclusion would actually matter:
# .env holds LITELLM_MASTER_KEY and CF_ACCESS_AUD_KEYPORTAL, and
# alertmanager.yml is rendered with a live webhook URL.
.env
versions.env
alertmanager/alertmanager.yml
